NAME
       dup, dup2 - duplicate a file descriptor

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       int dup(int oldfd);
       int dup2(int oldfd, int newfd);

DESCRIPTION
       Makes a second descriptor for the same open file. dup returns
       the lowest free number; dup2 uses NEWFD, closing it first if it
       was open.

       Both descriptors share the file offset, so a seek through one is
       seen by the other. This is how a shell wires redirection: dup2
       the opened file onto 0, 1 or 2 between fork and execve.

RETURN VALUE
       The new descriptor, or -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF   oldfd is not open, or newfd is out of range
       EMFILE  the process has no free descriptors

SEE ALSO
       pipe(2), open(2), close(2)
